component SigilLanguage {
  goal {
    Define the versioned source and interpretation contract for Sigil documents.
  }

  interface {
    SourceDocument {
      Accept UTF-8 `.sigil` sources containing *Component* or *Trait*
      declarations, *Contract* sections, *Concept* headings, blank-line *Facet*
      prose, *Inline Tag* and *Inline Link* prose, and *Embedded Facet*
      representations.
    }

    SourceGrammar {
      Give deterministic tools one structural grammar for declarations, imports,
      contracts, Concepts, Facets, and recoverable diagnostics.
    }

    ContractRoles {
      goal answers why; interface states promises and adopted concepts; state names
      meaningful modes or data; logic describes behavior and ordering; constraints
      bind invariants or prohibitions; decisions hold rationale and trade-offs; cases
      give a situation and observable outcome.

      A Case does not become a universal rule merely by appearing once; say whether
      its observed outcome is required or permitted.
    }
  }

  state {
    StructuralVocabulary {
      A declaration is a Component or Trait. A *Tag* is an Inline Tag or Concept.
      A Component may declare conformance to imported Traits.
    }
  }

  logic {
    SourceGrammar {
      Recognize only top-level imports followed by Components or Traits. A Component
      opens as `component Name {` or `component Name is Trait1, Trait2 {`; a Trait
      opens as `trait Name {`. Each declaration contains at most one of each allowed
      contract: goal, interface, state, logic, constraints, decisions, and cases.

      Recognize a Tag import as `@path/file.sigil from Component import { a, b }`.
      Recognize a Trait import as `@path/file.sigil import { Trait1, Trait2 }`.
      Both forms are file-scoped, name exact `.sigil` sources, and precede every
      declaration. No alias, wildcard, qualified reference, re-export, directory
      import, `expand`, or other declaration form exists.

      Recognize a Concept as a flat nonempty heading inside a contract. Repeated
      exact headings in one declaration gather Facets for one local Tag across
      contracts. A Concept heading never adopts an imported Tag.

      An Inline Tag definition is `*name*`, with no space beside either asterisk and
      the required outer boundaries in prose. `* name *` is not a definition. Tag
      names are case-sensitive and exact; tools do not normalize their whitespace or
      Unicode. Bare prose resolves the longest accessible Tag name. Links and fenced
      representations are opaque to Tag scanning.

      Join adjacent prose lines into one blank-line-delimited Facet. An Embedded
      Facet opens with three or more backticks, optionally followed by a type token,
      and closes with only at least as many backticks. It attaches directly to its
      introducing prose and preserves its literal body. Its labels and body create no
      Tags, Links, facts, or execution evidence.

      Preserve useful authored material and report malformed structure without
      inventing declarations or meaning.
    }

    TraitConformance {
      A Trait requires nonempty goal and interface; it may contain state,
      constraints, decisions, and cases, but never logic. A Component's `is` names
      imported Traits only. Conformed Trait obligations collect without override or
      order-based precedence.

      Trait interface, state, constraints, and cases contribute collectively to a
      conforming Component. Trait decisions remain rationale.

      A Component logic Concept supplies evidence for a Trait only when the heading
      exactly matches that Trait name and the Component declares conformance.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    SourceDocument {
      Every Component and Trait has nonempty goal and interface. Other contracts are
      optional and occur at most once in their declaration. Component names are
      workspace-unique by exact name.
    }

    TagOwnership {
      Each Component or Trait owns its local Tag vocabulary. Define each local Inline
      Tag once; retain the same exact Concept spelling and case when reusing it.
      Imported Tags cannot become local Concept headings. A bare Tag from another
      declaration is unavailable until selected by a Tag import.

      Interface introduces the Tags another Component must recognize and briefly says
      how each is adopted. A Tag introduced elsewhere and needed externally receives
      the same entry in interface.
    }

    ImportSemantics {
      Tag imports select Tags, including Concepts and state Tags, from the named
      owning Component.
      Trait imports select Traits without `from Component`. Duplicate, unused, or
      colliding imported names are errors. An import supplies vocabulary or
      conformance, not runtime access; contracts describe interactions.

      A selected Tag must occur in prose; a link label or fenced representation does
      not count. A Trait import is used by Component conformance. Imports never
      inherit a provider's imports. Import paths resolve from the workspace root.
    }

    LinkRoles {
      An Inline Link is `[label](destination)`. Its role is clear from surrounding
      prose: “must satisfy” can adopt a requirement, “follow” can offer guidance,
      and “explains why” can record rationale. These are examples, not reserved
      phrases. Relative targets resolve from their source; queries and fragments
      select within a target. The label or destination does not decide the role. An
      adopted link states its architectural rule; a platform or framework API remains
      explanatory rather than a binding implementation contract.
    }

    RepresentationBoundary {
      A representation communicates architecture rather than wire payloads, storage,
      framework calls, or executable implementation. Its labels do not establish
      Tags, facts, or execution evidence.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    SourceGrammar {
      Keep structural syntax deliberately small: natural language carries intent;
      declarations, ownership, and exact reusable names carry deterministic meaning.
    }
  }

  cases {
    TraitConformance {
      A Trait containing logic is invalid.

      A Component importing but not declaring a Trait does not conform to it.

      A Component declaring a Trait but using a differently named logic Concept does
      not supply that Trait evidence.
    }

    ImportSemantics {
      `@a.sigil from Provider import { status }` is a Tag import.

      `@a.sigil import { RequestSafety }` is a Trait import.

      `@a.md import { RequestSafety }` and `@a.sigil from Provider import { RequestSafety }`
      are invalid.
    }
  }
}
